<p>Hello Kiersten,</p>

<p>Thank you so much for your interest in sponsoring a blood drive with&nbsp;the American Red Cross. Every 2 seconds someone needs blood.&nbsp; We work hard to replenish the supply every single day of the year and I thank you for thinking of us. We are truly grateful when someone like you reaches out to us to offer help! This past year alone Hurricanes Harvey, Irma, Maria, and the tragedies&nbsp;in Las Vegas and Parkland, Florida have&nbsp;shown&nbsp;it is the blood on the shelves that is critical to meet the needs locally and across the country.&nbsp;I just left you a voice message but wanted to send you this information to get you started.</p>

<p>Please look at the two attachments. The first one is the important&nbsp;Blood Drive Interest Survey. This is to determine what sort of interest you have at your location for donating, and it will help us decide on a goal for your drive. &nbsp;We look for 40 names before we can confirm a date together for your drive. &nbsp;We also use the information to determine the size of the drive. &nbsp;Ask everyone if they are interested and jot down their name and contact info. The more names, the better! You might already know of 40 people interested! You also might want to enlist others to help spread the word and gather names of interested individuals. Feel free to use any method of communication that you feel will reach the most people.<br />
<br />
The second attachment is our Successful Blood Drive Guide. This is a simplified, step-by-step guide for success.</p>

<p>Once we determine there is sufficient interest, we&nbsp;would need to come out to your location to view where you&nbsp;would be holding the drive to do a site check. &nbsp;We look for a large open space for the drive.&nbsp;<br />
<br />
I will be in touch with you in a few days to see what sort of interest you have, and then we can proceed with looking at dates. In the meantime, please let me know if you have any questions.<br />
<br />
Thank you!</p>
Ann M. Wells<br />
Business Development Manager<br />
